SDSYS may use the API only from a process running as the sdsys user on this machine.

SDSYS can change every account on this system.  A loopback address does not
show who is at the other end - an ssh tunnel ends on this machine and looks
local - so SD asks the kernel which user opened the socket, and admits SDSYS
only when that user is sdsys itself.  Connect over SD's Unix socket from a
session running as sdsys, or run sd as the sdsys user at this machine.
